# Clustered light culling (ABI 1.21): a synthetic town at midnight, fog off.
# A 5 x 5 grid of blocks, each a pavement slab with four box buildings of
# varied height, between streets 4 units wide. 240 street lamps (thin posts,
# each with a point light 2.4 units up, range 3.5 to 5: mostly warm sodium,
# some cool white, a few pink, green and blue shop lights) line every street
# on alternating sides, and 16 spot lights shine down over the crossings.
# That is far past the 32 point and 32 spot lights STRATA_LIGHT_CULLING_NONE
# allows; with light_culling clustered each fragment evaluates only the lights
# listed for its cluster. The first lamp casts cube-map shadows, to show that
# shadowed lights keep working under clustered culling. Written by
# tools/gen_street_lights_scene.py --lamps 240 --spots 16; see docs/LIGHTING.md.
size 640 360
camera 0 34 40  0 0 -4  50 0.5 160
lighting sun 0.0 35  4 2048 80 0.6 0
ambient 0.25 0.3 0.45  0.004 0.005 0.009
clear 0.01 0.012 0.025 1
light_culling clustered
item cube 0 -0.5 0  72 1 72  0.22 0.22 0.24
